.TH DNET2.CONF 5 "September 2026" "dnet2-bpf" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
dnet2.conf \- settings for the dnet2 systemd service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/dnet2/dnet2.conf
is an EnvironmentFile read by the supplied
.B dnet2.service
unit.
It supplies command-line arguments to
.BR dnet2d (8).
The daemon does not read this file when invoked directly.
.SH FORMAT
Use one VARIABLE=value assignment per line.
Blank lines and comment lines beginning with a hash sign are permitted.
Quote values containing spaces, as shown below.
This file is not a shell script: do not use shell commands, command
substitution, or depend on shell variable expansion.
See
.BR systemd.exec (5)
for the full EnvironmentFile syntax.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B DNET2_IFACE_A
Physical interface for network A.
Shipped value: ens19.
.TP
.B DNET2_IFACE_B
Physical interface for network B.
Shipped value: ens20.
A and B must be distinct existing interfaces; do not use the management NIC.
In TAP mode, bring both links up before starting the service.
.TP
.B DNET2_VIRTUAL_OPTIONS
Optional TAP command-line arguments.
Shipped value: "\-v dnet2".
This creates adapter dnet2 with default address 172.23.1.1/16.
Add \-a address/prefix to override the startup address.
An empty or absent value selects legacy BPF cloning mode.
The service expands this value into separate arguments.
.TP
.B DNET2_RX_OBJECT
Legacy RX BPF object path.
Shipped value: /usr/local/lib/dnet2-bpf/dnet2_rx.bpf.o.
Ignored in TAP mode.
.TP
.B DNET2_TX_OBJECT
Legacy TX BPF object path.
Shipped value: /usr/local/lib/dnet2-bpf/dnet2_tx.bpf.o.
Ignored in TAP mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
Default topology: virtual network 172.23.0.0/16 carried over A on 172.21.*
and B on 172.22.*:
.PP
.nf
DNET2_IFACE_A=ens19
DNET2_IFACE_B=ens20
DNET2_VIRTUAL_OPTIONS="\-v dnet2"
DNET2_RX_OBJECT=/usr/local/lib/dnet2-bpf/dnet2_rx.bpf.o
DNET2_TX_OBJECT=/usr/local/lib/dnet2-bpf/dnet2_tx.bpf.o
.fi
.PP
Choose a different virtual host address:
.PP
.nf
DNET2_VIRTUAL_OPTIONS="\-v dnet2 \-a 172.23.1.2/16"
.fi
.PP
Select legacy mode:
.PP
.nf
DNET2_VIRTUAL_OPTIONS=
.fi
.SH APPLYING CHANGES
Restart the service after editing this file:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl restart dnet2
systemctl status dnet2
journalctl \-u dnet2 \-f
.fi
.PP
A daemon-reload is needed when the service unit changes, not for changes to
this environment file alone.
Restarting removes and recreates the TAP, discarding runtime adapter changes.
Use
.BR ip (8)
for temporary configuration while the daemon is running.
.PP
Installation preserves an existing configuration file.
When upgrading an older installation, add DNET2_VIRTUAL_OPTIONS explicitly
to enable the virtual adapter.
Uninstallation retains this file.
.SH NOTES
Use a unique virtual address for each host.
The daemon does not assign 172.21.* or 172.22.* addresses to the physical
interfaces; configure them through the host's normal network tools.
See
.BR dnet2d (8)
for transport limitations, required privileges, and recovery procedures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnet2d (8),
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ip (8)
